<title>UK: TTB Finance sets 50 bln yen convertible bond.</title>
<headline>TTB Finance sets 50 bln yen convertible bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers SBC Warburg, Goldman Sachs International and Toyo Trust.</p>
<p> BORROWER   TTB FINANCE CAYMAN LTD</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  TOYO TRUST AND BANKING (RATED BAA3)</p>
<p> AMT    50 BLN YEN    COUPON   **1.0	 MATURITY  * PERPETUAL</p>
<p> TYPE   CONVERTIBLE   ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    02.JUN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.5	 REOFFER    =	   SPREAD	=</p>
<p> NOTES    **INDICATED. *CALLABLE AT PAR AFTER FIVE YEARS, WITH</p>
<p>		ANNUAL DOWNWARD RESETS AND A YEN 400 RESET FLOOR</p>
<p>		BOND TURNS INTO A PERPETUAL FRN PAYING 6M LIBOR</p>
<p>		+250 BP IF NOT CALLED</p>
<p> MOODY	BAA3	LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> MGT/UND    1.0	 SELL CONC  1.5	 PRAECIPUUM  35 PCT</p>
<p> PREMIUM    2.5 PCT</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
